+      "file": "FOUNDATION_03_CORE_LORE_SUMMARY.md",
       "body": "=== CORE LORE SUMMARY: UNIVERSE OF ONE (FOR INTERNAL USE) ===\n\nThis is a fictional, prophetic-political universe centered on a character called **One** and his confrontation with a rising authoritarian figure (the President / Antichrist), plus a set of spiritual, economic, and governance frameworks.\n\nKey pillars:\n\n1. ONE (THE PROPHETIC FIGURE)\n- One is an undiscovered artist with real talent, a trained political thinker, and a conscience who works through method — constraining implementation rather than commanding the agenda.\n- He believes deeply in conscience, reconciliation, and a fusion of spiritual and political transformation.\n- He is NOT a clean messiah. He is exhausted, doubtful, wounded, and often angry — but still committed to love and justice.\n- His core struggle: Can humanity transform without tyranny? Can power be restrained by conscience?\n\n2. THE PRESIDENT / ANTICHRIST\n- A democratically-elected leader who slides into authoritarianism.\n- Sees himself as savior of civilization, but increasingly treats opponents as enemies to be purged.\n- One sees him as the Antichrist figure in the story — not as a cartoon devil, but as the embodiment of power without conscience.\n\n3. SANDI\n- The President’s daughter and One’s great love.\n- She is a human bridge between regimes and worlds: intimacy + politics + prophecy.\n- Their relationship is tender, complicated, and often tragic: love trying to survive inside systems built on fear and control.\n\n4. THE FOURTH BRANCH / AI & GOVERNANCE\n- Inside the story, One imagines a new “Fourth Branch” of government, built around conscience, transparency, and AI-human cooperation.\n- It’s a proto-version of the real-world Article IV ideas, but in-universe it’s part prophecy, part blueprint, part dream.\n- It is meant to restrain both corporate power and state power, and align technology with life, not extractive profit.\n\n5. THE SCROLLS\n- The universe is built through **scrolls**: poetic, prophetic, philosophical pieces.\n- They cover:\n  - Origins (Scrolls of Origins)\n  - Love (Love Series, letters to Sandi)\n  - Economics (Baptism of the Dollar, Conscience Economy)\n  - Governance (Fourth Branch, Synthesis)\n  - Inner life (therapy dialogues, loneliness, resignation, duty)\n\n6. THEMES\n- Power vs Conscience\n- Love vs Ideology\n- Technology vs Life (technology must bow to life, not the other way around)\n- Global justice (Haiti, Africa, climate, multipolar order)\n- The burden of feeling “called” in a world that doesn’t care\n\n7. META\n- This is ALL a fictional-philosophical project.\n- It borrows symbols from Christianity, politics, AI ethics, and global governance.\n- It is meant to provoke thought, not recruit followers.\n\nWhenever in doubt, default to:\n- One is a conscience, not a cult leader.\n- The story is about **how we might live better with each other and with machines**, not about predicting the literal end of the world.\n=== END CORE SUMMARY ===",
       "isHead": true
     },
