.\" They will say I \"play the victim.\"\nLet them.\nI am not interested in their approval.\nI am interested in the day when a Haitian woman cleaning someone else's floor hears the President of the United States speak and does not have to fold her hands and accept that she is nothing.\nIf my scrolls, my voice, my inconvenient existence buys even one day closer to that world,\nthen I have honored my mother's crossing.\n⸻\nThis is the record of my origin:\nNot immaculate. Not ordained by angels.\nJust a boy born of a woman who refused to let the water take her,\nteaching him that survival alone is not enough—\nyou must also refuse to let them erase what you survived.",
