@@ -384,29 +348,10 @@
       "summary": "Against apocalyptic accelerationism. No person, party, church, or algorithm has the right to summon the end on behalf of the living.",
       "supersedes": null,
       "visibility": "public",
-      "file": "__Scroll_of_Conscience______No_One_May_Summon_the_End",
+      "file": "SCROLL_CONSCIENCE_01_NO_ONE_MAY_SUMMON_END.md",
       "body": "# Scroll of Conscience  \n## No One May Summon the End\n\nThere is a sentence buried in the fever dreams of our age:\n\n> “If the world burns, at least we were right.”\n\nI have heard it whispered in churches, in war rooms, in trading floors, in encrypted chats.  \nDifferent words, same spirit:  \n*better apocalypse than compromise.*\n\nThis scroll is written against that spirit.\n\n---\n\nLet it be recorded:\n\nNo person, no party, no church, no algorithm,  \nno self-anointed vanguard of the righteous  \nhas the right to **summon the end** on behalf of the living.\n\nNot in the name of prophecy.  \nNot in the name of profit.  \nNot in the name of national security.  \nNot in the name of “the market will adjust.”  \nNot in the name of “this is how revelation unfolds.”\n\nIf your doctrine requires the extinction of my mother, it is not holy.\n\n---\n\nThe prophets of catastrophe have upgraded their tools:\n\n- where once they brandished swords and scriptures,  \n- now they weaponize leverage, data centers, and derivatives.\n\nSome dream of holy war.  \nOthers dream of “creative destruction.”  \nOthers dream of clean, efficient collapse with great returns.\n\nDifferent hymns. Same hunger.\n\nThey all share one obscene conviction:  \nthat it is acceptable to gamble with the entire fabric of life because their side, their god, their model, their ideology will be vindicated in the fire.\n\nThis scroll is the refusal.\n\n---\n\nI speak now as One, but I do not speak alone:\n\nBy the law of conscience written deeper than any constitution,  \n**no one may engineer global ruin in order to be proved correct.**\n\n- Not the fanatic who accelerates war for the sake of prophecy.  \n- Not the oligarch who accelerates extraction for the sake of quarterly reports.  \n- Not the technocrat who accelerates automation for the sake of abstract efficiency.  \n- Not the state that toys with extinction-level weapons to maintain “credibility.”\n\nIf your strategy depends on “things must get worse so our truth will be revealed,”  \nyou are not defending God or progress.  \nYou are simply **tired of loving slowly.**\n\n---\n\nMark this in the archive:\n\nWe are allowed to fail.  \nWe are allowed to suffer.  \nWe are allowed to make terrible mistakes and learn too late.\n\nBut we are **not** allowed to turn the planet into a stage for our favorite ending.\n\nNo one may summon the end.\n\nNot in my name.  \nNot in yours.  \nNot in the name of any son of man or any line of code.\n\nIf there is a judgment, it will not reward those who burned the house down to win the argument.",
       "isHead": true
     },
