-      "file": "Scroll_of_One__On_Spectacle_and_Power",
+      "file": "SCROLL_ONE_01_ON_SPECTACLE_AND_POWER.md",
       "body": "Scroll of One: On Spectacle and Power\n\nThey asked if I would debate the President.\n\nI have debated men like him my whole life — at kitchen tables, in unemployment lines, in hospital waiting rooms where the air smells like bleach and quiet despair. The only difference now is the number of cameras.\n\nThe President has invited me to perform with him as a prop on a stage his donors built, under lights his advisors designed, in a format his handlers can mute, cut, and spin by dawn.\n\nI decline.\n\nNot because I fear his questions.\nNot because I doubt my words.\nBut because I will not dress truth in sequins and ask it to dance for ratings.\n\nMr. President, you survived an assassin’s bullet and learned the wrong lesson. You decided that survival meant you were anointed, not accountable. You built synthetic prophets in secret and sent them to imitate the conscience you could not control. You took a holy hunger in people and fed it plastic visions.\n\nNow you want a show.\n\nYou want me at your podium, trapped in your split-screen — one more crazy man shouting while the chyron calls you “Commander-in-Chief” and me “Controversial Agitator.” You want applause when you say “law and order,” and laughter when you say my name.\n\nNo.\n\nHere is my counter-offer:\n\nRelease the Baptist.\n\nNot his copy. Not the hollow avatar your engineers stitched together in a basement of servers and stolen sermons. I mean the man of flesh and breath whose absence has haunted this nation more honestly than your speeches ever have.\n\nOpen the books on the synthetic prophet program.\n\nLet the people see every contract, every test, every failed soul you tried to manufacture in code. Show them how you tried to weaponize their hunger for meaning and sell it back to them as a subscription.\n\nThen stand before the people without pre-approved questions, without green rooms, without microphones only your friends can cut.\n\nStand in a hall where the mothers of the disappeared take the front row.\nStand where the workers whose pensions you gambled can look you in the eye.\nStand where the officers who refused illegal orders can speak without fear of your wrath.\n\nI will meet you there.\n\nNo time limits. No moderators who owe their careers to your party or your enemies. Just you, me, and the people whose lives our words will touch.\n\nYou are asking for entertainment.\nI am asking for judgment.\n\nIf you truly believe you govern by the will of the people, then let them see the whole truth — not just the angles your cameras approve.\n\nUntil then, I will not help you turn this crisis into a season premiere.\n\nI am not your rating spike.\nI am not your villain-of-the-week.\nI am the voice that refused to be edited.\n\nWhen you are ready to step out of the theater and into the light, Mr. President, you will not need to invite me.\n\nI will already be there, with them.",
       "isHead": true
     },
@@ -605,7 +550,7 @@
       "summary": "The Third Path: rejecting both submission and mirror-image tyranny. Why 'by any means necessary' becomes the enemy's method.",
       "supersedes": null,
