+      "file": "SCROLL_LOVE_01_QUIET_LOBBY.md",
       "body": "# Love Series  \n## Letter to Sandi I – The Quiet Lobby\n\nSandi,\n\nIf this reaches you, it will probably be in a quiet moment between meetings you didn’t ask for and obligations you never consented to.\n\nI imagine you in some high glass building,  \nfloors humming with policy and PR,  \nwearing a dress that fits the cameras better than it fits your mood.\n\nThey will say you were born into privilege.  \nI know you were born into crossfire.\n\n---\n\nWhen I met you, I did not know you were the President’s daughter.\n\nI just saw a woman who listened like the world was on trial  \nand she had been appointed its reluctant defender.\n\nYou laughed with your whole lungs,  \nbut your shoulders stayed ready for impact.\n\nI should have known then.\n\n---\n\nThis is not a strategic letter.\n\nIt will not help the polls.  \nIt will not heal the party.  \nIt will not make the markets less nervous.\n\nIt is simply this:\n\nI love the part of you that still believes tenderness is not a liability.\n\nThe part that aches watching security details bark at janitors.  \nThe part that notices who clears the coffee cups after the briefing.  \nThe part that cries in bathrooms not because you are weak,  \nbut because there is nowhere in the schedule to grieve.\n\n---\n\nThey tell you that love is a distraction.\n\nThey are wrong.\n\nLove is the only metric that has never lied to me.\n\n- When I see your eyes dim in staged photos, I know the regime is rotting, no matter what the numbers say.  \n- When you send a three-word message — *“Still watching. Still here.”* — after one of my scrolls goes viral, I know the resistance is alive, even if the streets are empty.\n\nYou are my most dangerous data point.\n\n---\n\nThere will come a day when they ask you to choose:\n\n- Father or future.  \n- Loyalty or life.  \n- Silence or scandal.\n\nWhen that day comes, this letter will not decide for you.\n\nI will not weaponize our love as leverage in your conscience.\n\nAll I ask is that you remember:\n\nYou were a human being before you were a symbol.  \nYou were a daughter before you were a bridge.  \nYou were a laughing, stubborn, inconvenient soul  \nbefore the cameras ever framed your face.\n\nIf you must betray someone,  \nlet it be the version of yourself that learned to tolerate cruelty for the sake of peace.\n\n---\n\nI do not know if we will ever walk freely in the same city again.\n\nBut if the day comes when power finally falls silent around you  \nand you are left alone with your own pulse,  \nI hope you hear this:\n\nYou were loved, not as a bargaining chip,  \nnot as a corridor into the palace,  \nbut as a woman who tried,  \nagainst terrible odds,  \nto remain kind in a building that monetized fear.\n\nThat alone, Sandi,  \nis already a revolution.",
       "isHead": true
     },
