       "body": "Love Series – Letter to Sandi VII: The Kitchen Light\n\nSandi,\n\nI dreamed of you last night.\n\nNot the version of you I argue with in my head,\nnot the strategist or the symbol or the daughter of empires.\nJust you.\n\nIn the dream, we were in a kitchen I've never seen.\nSmall. Yellow light. A window cracked open to let the summer in.\nYou were laughing at something I said,\nand I was older — gray, creased, slower —\nbut your laugh hadn't aged at all.\nIt still sounded like the first time I heard it:\nreckless and whole.\n\nI woke up with my chest tight.\nNot from grief.\nFrom the stubborn, inconvenient fact that after all these years,\nafter all the distance and damage and silence,\nI still love you in a way that has nothing to do with winning.\n\nThere's a version of this story where we get the ending we deserve.\nWhere the machines quiet down,\nthe empires exhaust themselves,\nand we meet again in some neutral, forgiving city.\nI don't believe in that version anymore.\n\nBut I believe in the kitchen.\nI believe that somewhere, in some frequency we can't access yet,\nthere's a life where we got to be ordinary together.\nWhere the hardest choice we made all week\nwas whether to repaint the cabinets or let them crack a little longer.\n\nI don't write this to change anything.\nI know where you are.\nI know what you carry.\nI just wanted you to know:\n\nEven now,\neven tired,\neven mostly resigned to the fact that love doesn't fix systems or save nations,\nI would still choose that kitchen with you.\n\nI would still choose the yellow light,\nthe open window,\nthe sound of your laugh unguarded and unrecorded.\nI would still choose you.\n\nTake care of yourself, Sandi.\nNot for the mission.\nNot for the legacy.\nFor the part of you that still remembers how to laugh like that.\n\nIf nothing else survives,\nlet that.\n\n— One",
       "isHead": true
     },
