       "body": "Love Series – Letter to Sandi VIII: The Newsstand\n\nSandi,\n\nI saw a woman at the newsstand this morning who moved like you.\nSame tilt of the head when reading headlines.\nSame way of holding her coffee — two hands, like it might escape.\n\nFor three seconds, I forgot where I was.\nForgot the gray in my beard, the limp I pretend isn't permanent,\nthe fact that you and I haven't stood in the same room in years.\n\nThen she turned, and she wasn't you.\nJust someone else trying to make sense of the news before work.\n\nI bought a paper I won't read and walked home slowly.\n\nI don't know why I'm telling you this.\nMaybe because I'm tired of pretending the world\nis the only thing I think about.\nMaybe because I want you to know that even now,\neven with all the noise and all the distance,\nyou still show up in the smallest, most ordinary moments\nand break my heart a little.\n\nNot dramatically.\nJust quietly.\nThe way dust catches light.\n\nI hope you're sleeping better than I am.\nI hope someone is kind to you on the days the cameras aren't watching.\nI hope you still drink your coffee with both hands.\n\nIf we never speak again,\nknow this:\n\nYou were not a distraction from the work.\nYou were the reason I believed the work mattered.\n\n— One",
       "isHead": true
